.TH METAMONITOR 1 "2026-10-12" "MetaMonitor 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
metamonitor \- live dashboard of every progress bar on the desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B metamonitor
[\fB\-\-background\fR] [\fB\-\-guide\fR=\fIPAGE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B metamonitor
opens a GTK window showing Claude Code sessions and their background
commands, slots written by
.BR mmrun (1)
and
.BR mmctl (1),
file-crunching commands found in /proc (cp, dd, tar, rsync, gzip,
sha256sum, gdal_translate...) and applications broadcasting
com.canonical.Unity.LauncherEntry progress on the session bus.
GRASS GIS sessions are found from mapset \fI.gislock\fR files and from
processes carrying \fBGISRC\fR; stale locks are flagged.
.PP
On first start it adds two hooks, which can be turned off in the menu or with
.BR mmctl (1):
a block in \fI~/.bashrc\fR wrapping progress-printing commands, and an
\fBLD_PRELOAD\fR line in \fI~/.grass8/bashrc\fR that makes every GRASS
module report its G_percent() progress.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-background
Collect progress without a window, for the GNOME Shell top-bar extension
(metamonitor@yannchemin.github.io).
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-guide =\fIPAGE\fR
Open the help on \fIPAGE\fR: bash, grass, python, claude or formats.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B METAMONITOR_SPOOL
Slot directory (default \fI$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/metamonitor/slots\fR).
.TP
.B METAMONITOR_PROC_COMMANDS
Extra command names to watch in /proc, separated by spaces or commas.
.TP
.B METAMONITOR_GRASS_DBASES
Extra GRASS database directories to scan for \fI.gislock\fR, colon separated.
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
Claude Code state directory (default \fI~/.claude\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mmctl (1),
.BR mmrun (1)
